			"offsets": {
				"from": 201460,
				"to": 203480
			},
			"text": " Well, not exactly once a year."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:23,480",
				"to": "00:03:26,860"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 203480,
				"to": 206860
			},
			"text": " The momentum of the atmospheric winds would get transferred back to the Earth, starting"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:26,860",
				"to": "00:03:31,020"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 206860,
				"to": 211020
			},
			"text": " at spinning again very slowly since the atmosphere is much lighter than the Earth."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:31,020",
				"to": "00:03:35,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 211020,
				"to": 215540
			},
			"text": " Relative to the distant stars, a single spin of the Earth would now take around 3,000 years"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:35,540",
				"to": "00:03:36,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 215540,
				"to": 216540
			},
			"text": " to complete."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:36,540",
				"to": "00:03:41,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 216540,
				"to": 221060
			},
			"text": " So for all practical purposes, the once-per-orbit day that lasts a year would win out."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:41,060",
				"to": "00:03:44,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 221060,
				"to": 224060
			},
			"text": " Earth would experience six months of daylight and six months of night."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:44,060",
				"to": "00:03:47,500"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 224060,
				"to": 227500
			},
			"text": " On the day side, the surface would bake under the constant sunlight, while on the night side,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:47,500",
				"to": "00:03:48,940"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 227500,
				"to": 228940
			},
			"text": " the temperature would plummet."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:48,940",
				"to": "00:03:51,980"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 228940,
				"to": 231980
			},
			"text": " Although the length of the day would change, the length of the month would not."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:51,980",
				"to": "00:03:54,260"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 231980,
				"to": 234260
			},
			"text": " The moon hasn't stopped revolving around the Earth."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:54,260",
				"to": "00:03:59,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 234260,
				"to": 239460
			},
			"text": " In fact, the moon, our faithful companion, would act to partly undo what Andrew has done."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:59,460",
				"to": "00:04:01,620"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 239460,
				"to": 241620
			},
			"text": " Remember, this is all Andrew's fault."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:01,620",
				"to": "00:04:05,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 241620,
				"to": 245460
			},
			"text": " Before Andrew, the Earth's tidal bulge created by the moon's gravity slowed down our rotation"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:05,460",
				"to": "00:04:07,740"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 245460,
				"to": 247740
			},
			"text": " while dragging the moon into a higher orbit."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:07,740",
				"to": "00:04:11,140"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 247740,
				"to": 251140
			},
			"text": " After Andrew stopped the Earth's rotation, the moon's gravity would tug on the Earth"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:11,140",
				"to": "00:04:17,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 251140,
				"to": 257800
			},
			"text": " and very, very, very gradually speed us up again just a little while it slowed down."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:17,800",
				"to": "00:04:22,260"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 257800,
				"to": 262260
			},
			"text": " While eventually, someone could again ask, \"What if the Earth suddenly stopped rotating?\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:04:22,260",
				"to": "00:04:23,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 262260,
				"to": 263060
			},
			"text": " Thank you, moon."
		}
	]
}
